# Differential cases (ADR-0020) of #65 "S2a.15 Arithmetic and computed numbers": every operator on every pair of
# kinds, one value of each kind (null, false, true, 1, "a", [1], {"a":1}), both read from one document as .[0] OP
# .[1], with jq's error texts; then the 29-byte cut of a value in those texts (jv_dump_string_trunc, ErrorDump): a
# dump of 29 bytes shows whole, a longer one keeps 25 bytes (26 for a number) and ends in ...", ...] or ...}, stepping
# back to a character start but not to an escape start. Written by a script from the product of the kinds; Format:
# oracle/src/main/java/io/github/subapavel/jqj/oracle/diff/DiffCase.java. Expected outputs live in arith-kinds.rec,
# written by scripts/oracle-record.sh only. Ids are immutable.

# plus

case arith-kinds/plus-null-null
arg -c
filter .[0] + .[1]
stdin [null,null]\n
end

case arith-kinds/plus-null-false
arg -c
